{"study_accession":"PRJNA704395","secondary_study_accession":"SRP307775","title":"GM-CSF-induced CD40high human blood dendritic cells promote Tfh1 polarization","description":"Using single-cell RNA sequencing (10X technology) on CD4+T cells, we report that GM-CSF-activated human blood CD1c+ dendritic cells (DC) (cDC2) drive the differentiation of naïve CD4+ T cells into Tfh1. These Tfh1 cells displayed typical Tfh molecular features, including high levels of PD-1, CXCR5, and ICOS. They co-expressed Bcl6 and T-bet, and secreted large amounts of IL-21 and IFN-γ. Overall design: We performed single cell RNA sequencing using 10X Chromium technology on CD4+ T cells previously co-cultured with three different DC activation conditions (GM-CSF-activated-DC, LPS-activated-DC and Medium-activated-DC). The protocol is detailed below.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":3,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN18039745","study_accession":"PRJNA704395","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"GM-CSF-activated_blood_DC-polarized_CD4_T_cells","description":"GM-CSF-activated_blood_DC-polarized_CD4_T_cells","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5102908","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":4,"first_public":"2021-10-02","attributes":[["source_name","Activated CD4+Tcells"],["co-culture condition","GM-CSF-activated_blood_DC-polarized_CD4_T_cells"],["dataset name","GM-CSF-activated_blood_DC-polarized_CD4_T_cells"],["cell_type","CD4+Tcells"],["tissue","Blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13772220","experiment_accession":"SRX10157891","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":597,"base_count":40365,"first_public":"2021-10-02","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5102908: GM-CSF-activated_blood_DC-polarized_CD4_T_cells Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR13772221","experiment_accession":"SRX10157891","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model